   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to requiring that the annual\nreport from the division of minority and women's business development contain\ninformation on the annual minority and women-owned business enterprise\nutilization and expenditure categorized by minority-owned enterprises,\nwomen-owned enterprises, and total utilization and expenditure, and be\norganized by certain industry categories",
    "basePrintNo": "S8815",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8815-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §315, Exec L (as proposed in S.8393 & A.7222)",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8815\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to requiring that the\nannual report from the division of minority and women's business devel-\nopment contain information on the annual minority and women-owned busi-\nness enterprise utilization and expenditure categorized by minority-\nowned enterprises, women-owned enterprises, and total utilization and\nexpenditure, and be organized by certain industry categories\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to L.2025, C.661\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by removing a breakdown\nof the reported information by minority groups, by removing reporting on\nspecific contracts and clarifying the industry type breakdown of the\nutilization information in the report.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 661 of the Laws of 2025.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nChapter of the Laws of 2025 amending the executive law relating to\nrequirements of the annual report from the division of minority and\nwomen's business development, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\n5.8393 and A.7222, takes effect.\n",
